<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Domingo Paes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Domingo Paes was a Portuguese traveller and horse trader who visited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> around 1520, during the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a>. His detailed account of the capital, its palaces, markets and temples and the Mahanavami festival, is one of the main sources for the city at its height. It survives in a sixteenth-century compilation together with the chronicle of Fernão Nunes.</p></div>
